# Scripts start with a shebang and several are imported by tests. Vitest strips the shebang with a
# regex whose `.` stops at a CR, so a CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) left `#!` in the
# module and the importing test failed with a SyntaxError. LF on every checkout (as in the core).
scripts/*.mjs text eol=lf
